{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments ["<b>And they shall fill your houses and the houses of all your servants and the houses of all Egypt.</b> Without doubt the king's house is more inner than the houses of all his servants, and the houses of all his servants are more inner than the houses of all Egypt — so how could the locusts enter first into the innermost chambers and only afterward at the head of all the streets? Rather, this was certainly done by way of a miracle, for the measure of punishment corresponds to the measure of the sin: he began the corruption first, and afterward his servants — for without doubt he attributed the sin more to himself than to his servants, and more to his servants than to all his people — in the manner that Rashi explained concerning the frogs (Exodus 7:28), where it is said: ״וְעָלוּ וּבָאוּ בְּבֵיתֶךָ וְגוֹ׳ וּבְבֵית עֲבָדֶיךָ וּבְעַמֶּךָ״. And perhaps it is concerning this inverted order that it was said ״לְפָנָיו לֹא הָיָה כֵן אַרְבֶּה כָּמֹהוּ״ — it is possible that there was locusts like them, but never so on this reversed order, contrary to the way of the world." "<b>And he turned and went out from Pharaoh.</b> It is possible to explain that he had not yet gone out; rather, he turned his face away from him to depart, and he only went out from Pharaoh's presence, but he was still among his servants. And in the midst of this, ״וַיֹּאמְרוּ עַבְדֵי פַרְעֹה אֵלָיו עַד מָתַי יִהְיֶה זֶה לָנוּ לְמוֹקֵשׁ״ (Exodus 10:7) — they were pointing at Moses with their finger, saying: this man Moses — we do not know how long he will be a snare to us. And from their saying ״זֶה״ — 'this one' — we infer that he was still among them. Therefore ״וַיּוּשַׁב אֶת מֹשֶׁה וְאֶת אַהֲרֹן״ (Exodus 10:8) — they were brought back of themselves, for he did not send after them, since they were still among them and heard the words of the servants; and on that account they were brought back and returned to Pharaoh, ״וַיֹּאמֶר אֲלֵהֶם לְכוּ עִבְדוּ״ וְגוֹ׳ (Exodus 10:8)."], :book :exodus, :voice :kli-yakar, :lang :en, :chapter 10, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:18:59.045024063Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}